title: Passive resistance
subtitle: 13 January. Cuno asks the Reichstag to stand behind him.
new-page: true
tags: kpd_event
view-if: year = 1923 and (month >= 2 or jan_week >= 2) and y23_ruhr_done = 1 and y23_passive_done = 0
on-arrival: y23_passive_done = 1

= The nation's front

Chancellor Cuno tells the Reichstag that Germany will not work for the occupiers. Officials, railwaymen and miners are to refuse every order of the French, and the Reich will pay for the strike. Every bourgeois party, from the Democrats to the German Nationals, rises behind him, and so does the SPD, which calls it the defence of the Republic. The völkisch benches applaud loudest of all.

The party alone has to decide whether the workers' place is in this national front, with the men who will make them pay for it.

{!<div class="kpd-insert" data-insert="vote" data-arg="ruhr"></div>!}

- @no: Vote no. The enemy is also at home.
